* SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
* Bilingual-port front end: architecture and component-level study models.
* NOT vendor macromodels. Transistor cards are written from datasheet headline
* numbers (fT, Ccb, hFE); every value is [verify]. See ../README.md.
*
* Decks must define models QN and QP before including this file (run.py does).

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- cable ---
* One conductor, 0.5 m: 55 ohm to ground (110 ohm differential, uncoupled
* conductors as in soft-phy-afe), 5.05 ns/m, plus an R-L ladder fitted to the
* 1394a cable attenuation limit (2.3/3.2/5.8 dB at 100/200/400 MHz for 4.5 m).
* The fit and its sqrt(f) extrapolation above 400 MHz are assumptions.
.subckt cseg a b
T1 a 0 m 0 Z0=55 TD=2.525n
R0 m m1 0.692
R1 m1 m2 1.62
L1 m1 m2 12.9n
R2 m2 m3 4.23
L2 m2 m3 2.69n
R3 m3 b 8.49
L3 m3 b 2.25n
.ends cseg

.subckt cond a b
X1 a n1 cseg
X2 n1 n2 cseg
X3 n2 n3 cseg
X4 n3 n4 cseg
X5 n4 n5 cseg
X6 n5 n6 cseg
X7 n6 n7 cseg
X8 n7 n8 cseg
X9 n8 b cseg
.ends cond

* 4.5 m pair: p,n at one end, q,r at the other.
.subckt cable p n q r
Xp p q cond
Xn n r cond
.ends cable

* ----------------------------------------------------------------- peer ---
* Peer TPA side (faces our TPB): 2x55 ohm to its TPBIAS, 1 uF, 5 ohm source
* impedance (assumption), 5 pF per conductor input loading.
.subckt peer_tpa p n bias
Rp p ct 55
Rn n ct 55
Rb bias ct 5
Cb ct 0 1u
Cp p 0 5p
Cn n 0 5p
.ends peer_tpa

* Peer TPB side (faces our TPA): 2x55 ohm to 5k || 270 pF.
.subckt peer_tpb p n
Rp p ct 55
Rn n ct 55
Rg ct 0 5k
Cg ct 0 270p
Cp p 0 5p
Cn n 0 5p
.ends peer_tpb

* Ideal peer driver: differential current amp*cmd (cmd -1/0/1) and a
* per-conductor common-mode sink v(sp) amperes (speed signal or imbalance).
.subckt idrv p n cmd sp params: amp=4m
Bsig n p I={amp*v(cmd)}
Bsp p 0 I={v(sp)}
Bsn n 0 I={v(sp)}
Rout p n 100k
.ends idrv

* ------------------------------------------------------- our front end ---
* FPGA pad: ideal logic source "d" behind ron, 6 pF at the pad.
* ron = 22 ohm is an assumed LVCMOS33 16 mA output resistance [verify].
* ron = 3.3k with d = 0 models the 1 mA worst-case hot-socket leakage of an
* unpowered ECP5 top/bottom-bank pin; ron = 1g models a tri-stated pin.

* Bias references: one PNP and one NPN diode-connected reference, each fed
* through the same pad + emitter resistor as a driver leg so pad resistance
* and Vbe track. Released pads let 100k park VBP at VDD and VBN at ground.
.subckt refs vdd vbp vbn params: ron=22 re=91 rset=499
Bh h1 0 V={v(vdd)}
Rh1 h1 hp {ron}
Rep hp ep {re}
Qpr vbp vbp ep QP
Rsp vbp lp {rset}
Rl1 lp 0 {ron}
Rh2 h1 hn {ron}
Rsn hn vbn {rset}
Qnr vbn vbn en QN
Ren en ln {re}
Rl2 ln 0 {ron}
Rpu vbp vdd 100k
Rpd vbn 0 100k
Cbp vbp 0 100n
Cbn vbn 0 100n
.ends refs

* Driver legs for one pair. dsp/dsn: PNP source pads for P/N (high = on).
* dkp/dkn: NPN sink pads for P/N (low = on).
.subckt legs p n vbp vbn dsp dsn dkp dkn params: ron=22 re=91 ce=4.7p
Rosp dsp xsp {ron}
Cxsp xsp 0 6p
Resp xsp esp {re}
Cesp xsp esp {ce}
Qsp p vbp esp QP
Rosn dsn xsn {ron}
Cxsn xsn 0 6p
Resn xsn esn {re}
Cesn xsn esn {ce}
Qsn n vbp esn QP
Rokp dkp xkp {ron}
Cxkp xkp 0 6p
Rekp xkp ekp {re}
Cekp xkp ekp {ce}
Qkp p vbn ekp QN
Rokn dkn xkn {ron}
Cxkn xkn 0 6p
Rekn xkn ekn {re}
Cekn xkn ekn {ce}
Qkn n vbn ekn QN
.ends legs

* S200 and S400 speed-signal sinks on TPB. d2 = S200 pads, d4 = extra S400
* pads (S400 = both on). Low = on. One pad per conductor per level.
.subckt speed p n vbn d2p d2n d4p d4n params: ron=22 r2=100 r4=47
Ro2p d2p x2p {ron}
Re2p x2p e2p {r2}
Q2p p vbn e2p QN
Ro2n d2n x2n {ron}
Re2n x2n e2n {r2}
Q2n n vbn e2n QN
Ro4p d4p x4p {ron}
Re4p x4p e4p {r4}
Q4p p vbn e4p QN
Ro4n d4n x4n {ron}
Re4n x4n e4n {r4}
Q4n n vbn e4n QN
.ends speed

* Everything that hangs on one pair besides drivers and termination:
* SN65LVDS34 input (5 pF, 120k = 20 uA at 2.4 V), ESD array 0.5 pF, pads and
* stubs 1.5 pF, and the two arbitration comparators with resistive offset
* networks (threshold = VDD*ra/rb, about 124 mV). Comparator inputs are 3 pF
* with clamp diodes to VDD, which matter when the board is unpowered.
* Outputs: (app-apn) > 0 means "1", (anp-ann) > 0 means "0".
.model DCLAMP D (IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=10 CJO=0)
.subckt loads p n vdd app apn anp ann params: ra=10k rb=267k cpar=7p
Cp p 0 {cpar}
Cn n 0 {cpar}
Rlp p 0 120k
Rln n 0 120k
* positive comparator: + = k*p, - = k*n + (1-k)*VDD
Ra1 p app {ra}
Rb1 app 0 {rb}
Ra2 n apn {ra}
Rb2 apn vdd {rb}
* negative comparator: + = k*n, - = k*p + (1-k)*VDD
Ra3 n anp {ra}
Rb3 anp 0 {rb}
Ra4 p ann {ra}
Rb4 ann vdd {rb}
C1 app 0 3p
C2 apn 0 3p
C3 anp 0 3p
C4 ann 0 3p
D1 app vdd DCLAMP
D2 apn vdd DCLAMP
D3 anp vdd DCLAMP
D4 ann vdd DCLAMP
.ends loads

* Our TPA termination: 2x54.9 ohm to the TPBIAS node (1 uF), plus the
* common-mode sense (2x10k, 3 pF) used by the speed-detect comparators.
.subckt term_a p n bias cm
Rp p bias 54.9
Rn n bias 54.9
Cb bias 0 1u
Rcp p cm 10k
Rcn n cm 10k
Ccm cm 0 3p
.ends term_a

* Our TPB termination: 2x54.9 ohm to 5k || 270 pF, plus the slow common-mode
* sense (2x100k) used by the bias-detect comparator.
.subckt term_b p n ct cm
Rp p ct 54.9
Rn n ct 54.9
Rg ct 0 5k
Cg ct 0 270p
Rcp p cm 100k
Rcn n cm 100k
Ccm cm 0 10p
.ends term_b

* SerDes transmit branch on TPB: 10 nF blocking capacitors and 75 ohm pads.
* sp/sn are the SerDes pins (2 pF each, assumption for TLK1221/ECP5 [verify]).
.subckt sd_tx p n sp sn params: rs=75
Ccp p a 10n
Ccn n b 10n
Rsp a sp {rs}
Rsn b sn {rs}
Cpp sp 0 2p
Cpn sn 0 2p
Rlp sp 0 1meg
Rln sn 0 1meg
.ends sd_tx

* SerDes receive branch on TPA: 10 nF blocking capacitors into high-impedance
* pins biased by 3k to 1.5 V (TLK1221 figure 11 network, Thevenin).
.subckt sd_rx p n sp sn
Ccp p sp 10n
Ccn n sn 10n
Cpp sp 0 2p
Cpn sn 0 2p
Vb vb 0 1.5
Rbp sp vb 3k
Rbn sn vb 3k
.ends sd_rx

* Optional 2:1 switch, one differential channel, behavioural: 6 ohm on
* resistance, 1.5 pF each side when on, 1 pF stub for the off port. Values
* are typical of USB 3 class switches, not a specific part [verify].
.subckt mux_on a b
Ca a 0 1.5p
Coff a 0 1p
R a b 6
Cb b 0 1.5p
.ends mux_on
